## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design cross‑protocol data models and error handling for a basic user service, focusing on practical adapters rather than theory.

## Key Concepts

- Canonical schema and protobuf/DTO alignment
- Idempotency across REST, GraphQL, gRPC
- Unified error envelope and cross‑protocol mapping
- Minimal OpenAPI contract and adapter wiring

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo backend upsert by externalId
async function upsertUserProfile(externalId, payload) {
  const existing = await db.findByExternalId(externalId);
  if (existing) return await db.update(existing.id, payload);
  return await db.create({ externalId, ...payload });
}
```

